---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import logo from "../../assets/negahban.png";
import PageHeader from "../../components/PageHeader.astro";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
	title="negahban – Instagram comment watchman"
	description="negahban is a self-hosted command-line tool that moderates the comments on your own Instagram posts through Meta's official Instagram API."
>
	<Image
		src={logo}
		alt="negahban: a panda on sentry duty"
		width={192}
		height={192}
		class="logo-rounded"
	/>
	<PageHeader
		eyebrow="Side project"
		title="negahban"
		lede="A self-hosted command-line tool that keeps watch over the comments on your own Instagram posts."
	/>

	<div class="prose">
		<p>
			<b>negahban</b> (<span dir="rtl" lang="fa">نگهبان</span>, Persian for <i>watchman</i>)
			reads new comments through Meta's official Instagram API, asks an AI model
			what each one is (fine, civil criticism, abuse, spam, or a scam) and hides
			the abusive and junk ones. Civil criticism is never hidden, every decision
			is written to a local audit log, and every hide can be undone.
		</p>

		<h3>How it works</h3>
		<ol>
			<li>Connect your Instagram professional account (<code>negahban auth</code>).</li>
			<li>
				Run <code>negahban scan</code>: new comments on your recent posts are
				fetched and classified. By default this is a dry run that only reports.
			</li>
			<li>
				Run <code>negahban scan --apply</code> to hide abusive and spam comments.
				Low-confidence verdicts are only flagged for you.
			</li>
			<li>
				<code>negahban log</code> shows what was decided;
				<code>negahban unhide &lt;id&gt;</code> reverses a hide.
			</li>
		</ol>

		<h3>Links</h3>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<a href="https://github.com/parham-alvani/negahban" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
					Source code on GitHub
				</a>
			</li>
			<li><a href="/negahban/privacy">Privacy policy</a></li>
			<li><a href="/negahban/privacy#deletion">Data deletion</a></li>
			<li><a href="/negahban/privacy#terms">Terms of use</a></li>
		</ul>

		<h3>Contact</h3>
		<p>Elaheh Dastan, <b>elahe.dstn at gmail dot com</b></p>
	</div>
</Layout>
